      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "BLK_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_CONCEPTS_01",
          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR__FCA3AFA8_1",
          "title": "1. Key Academic Principles: Static, Kinetic & Rolling Friction",
          "contentMarkdown": "Friction is the tangential contact force opposing relative motion or the tendency of relative motion between two contacting surfaces. Static friction is a self-adjusting force whose maximum limiting value is fs_max = mu_s * N. Kinetic friction comes into play during relative sliding motion with magnitude fk = mu_k * N.",
          "boundAtomicFactIds": [
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_C845285E",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_EFCADA71",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_0D8F85C4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "BLK_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_CONCEPTS_02",
          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR__FCA3AFA8_2",
          "title": "2. Key Academic Principles: Static, Kinetic & Rolling Friction",
          "contentMarkdown": "The coefficient of kinetic friction mu_k is generally less than the coefficient of static friction mu_s. Rolling friction is significantly smaller than sliding friction because contact deformation is minimal during rolling. Methods of reducing friction include lubrication, polishing contact surfaces, and using ball bearings.",
          "boundAtomicFactIds": [
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_F06CFA99",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_F0F6523D",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_3B7C1EB0"
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "BLK_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_CONCEPTS_03",
          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR__FCA3AFA8_3",
          "title": "3. Key Academic Principles: Static, Kinetic & Rolling Friction",
          "contentMarkdown": "In general, mu_k is slightly less than mu_s. Kinetic friction is largely independent of the area of contact and relative velocity (within moderate speed ranges). Rolling Friction occurs when an object (like a cylinder or sphere) rolls without slipping over a flat surface.",
          "boundAtomicFactIds": [
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_8147C464",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_509F83E2",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_FCA3AFA8_8EDD52E7"
          ]
        }
      ],
